        {
          "check": "concurrency.if-match-enforced",
          "detail": "the record was read with ETag \"ETAG\" and updated under If-Match: \"ETAG\", which moved its ETag to \"ETAG\". A second update under the same If-Match: \"ETAG\", a version the record no longer has, answered 200, and the record's ETag moved again, to \"ETAG\". RFC 9110 requires a 412 when If-Match names no current version, so a client relying on it to keep from overwriting another's change overwrites it, and is told the write succeeded.",
